      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Definition"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "A question tag converts a declarative or imperative statement into a confirmation question.",
        "A positive clause always takes a negative question tag, while a negative clause requires a positive tag.",
        "The pronoun in the tag must match the subject in number, person, and gender.",
        "If no auxiliary verb is present in the main clause, 'do', 'does', or 'did' is used in the tag.",
        "Negative question tags must always use contracted forms (e.g., aren't, don't, didn't)."
      ],
      "id": "5zzkz9v"
    },
